[227.711028, "o", "## Done — all 13 tests green (clean build), golden master byte-identical.\r\n\r\n**Last-mile trace** — one Aged Brie through the chain (`GildedRose.java:22-29`):\r\n\r\n1. `updateQuality()` → `apply(item)` per item.\r\n"]
[227.712357, "o", "2. Chain iterates `AgedBrieUpdater → BackstagePassUpdater → SulfurasUpdater → RegularUpdater`.\r\n3. `AgedBrieUpdater.canHandle` matches `\"Aged Brie\"` → true → its `update` runs (quality+1, sellIn-1, double after expiry) → `return`.\r\n4. A `\"Conjured Mana Cake\"` falls past the three name-matching rules to the always-true `RegularUpdater` tail.\r\n\r\n**What changed** (Parallel Change):\r\n\r\n| File | Milestone |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `ItemUpdater.java` + 4 rule shells (`AgedBrieUpdater`, `BackstagePassUpdater`, `SulfurasUpdater`, `RegularUpdater`) | M1 Expand |\r\n| Each rule: `move_method` + rename→`update` + `final/public @Override` | M2 Migrate |\r\n| `GildedRose.java` — if/else ladder & 3 name constants replaced by one `List<ItemUpdater>` chain | M3 Contract |\r\n\r\nOne honesty note: my M2 verifications passed without a clean build, and the Regular-branch rewire was actually missing on disk — `mvn clean test` caught it, and the M3 contract write (per AGENTS.md's target state) fixed it. Every check since uses `mv"]
[227.712398, "o", "n clean test`.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
